        "selected_solver": "REMORA",
        "modifications": [],
        "reasoning": "The Taylor-Green Vortex (TGV) is a classic test case for validating numerical methods in fluid dynamics. Choosing a 2pi x 2pi x 2pi triply periodic domain allows for easy implementation of boundary conditions. A 64^3 grid provides sufficient resolution for capturing the flow dynamics. Re=1600 and nu=1/1600 are chosen to match the desired Reynolds number. Initializing with the standard TGV velocity field ensures a well-defined starting condition. Omitting the SGS model, Coriolis term, and gravity simplifies the simulation. Using 3rd-order advection and CFL<=0.5 helps ensure numerical stability and accuracy. Running the simulation to t=20 allows for the flow to develop and exhibit its characteristic features. Baseline weights: configuration_complexity=0.100, development_activity=0.100, domain_models=0.100, grid_specifications=0.200, path_hierarchy=0.150, physics_parameters=0.300, resource_requirements=0.050.",
